provenance.prompt:
Create an original 1536×1024 transparent RGBA 2D pixel-art sprite sheet for JAMVERSE '96: Echo Catwalk of Neo Runway Precision performing a right-facing basketball chest pass. Arrange exactly six separate complete full-body poses in a strict three-column by two-row grid, row-major. Keep each pose entirely within its own cell with broad transparent gutters and outer margins. Same camera, scale, feet baseline, anatomy and identity across all poses. No cell borders, court, floor, shadows, glow, text, ball, prop, teammate, opponent, hoop or rim.

Echo is a compact athletic adult human man with medium-brown skin, short spiky-curly dark-teal hair, a teal forehead band, neatly trimmed dark-teal beard and distinct focused face. He wears a sleeveless teal basketball jersey and shorts with black and deep-purple accents, black knee pads, teal-black basketball shoes and simple wristbands. Preserve his exact adult human anatomy, individual face, short dark-teal hair, forehead band, trimmed beard, teal/violet uniform palette, knee pads and shoes in every pose. He is not a woman, child, robot or creature. Show exactly two natural arms, two hands, two legs and two shoes. Keep both hands empty because the basketball is a separate game object. Never draw a ball, sphere, orb, seams or prop.

This is a quick chest pass delivered to a teammate on image-right. Six mechanically connected but distinct full-body poses:
0 balanced ready stance, elbows bent, empty hands framing the invisible ball at the sternum;
1 gathers both empty hands toward the chest, knees flex, weight settles back;
2 steps toward image-right, torso turns slightly toward target, elbows begin extending;
3 RELEASE at simulation tick5: lead arm extends straight toward image-right, wrist flicked, palm open and empty; trailing hand opens away from the invisible ball;
4 controlled full forward follow-through, body leans into the step and fingers extend;
5 balanced recovery with arms lowering naturally, feet stable, both hands empty.

Keep every pose right-facing, moving toward image-right. The separate basketball is never drawn. Draw six clean, unique silhouettes at consistent scale with complete hair, hands and shoes inside each cell. Crisp 1990s arcade pixel clusters, sharp outlines, readable at small gameplay scale, true transparent RGBA gutters and exterior; no alpha haze, checkerboard or matte. Return only the sprite sheet.
